   "daf": "61b",
   "sentenceId": 16,
   "he": "הַתַּלְמִידִים יוֹצְאִין לְתַלְמוּד וְכוּ׳. בִּרְשׁוּת כַּמָּה? כַּמָּה דְּבָעֵי.",
   "en": "§ The mishna said that «students may leave» their homes and travel for up to thirty days in order «to learn Torah,» without their wives’ permission. The Gemara asks: If they went «with permission,» for «how long» can they go? The Gemara expresses wonderment at this question: If they went with the permission of their wives, they can go for «as long as they want.» If the husband and wife agree on this, why is there any reason for the court to intervene?"
  }
